<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ambrogio Contarini</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1429">1429</a>–<a href="/years/1499">1499</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ambrogio Contarini was a Venetian merchant and diplomat sent in 1474 as ambassador to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan">Uzun Hasan</a>, to seek an alliance against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. He travelled through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and returned by way of Muscovy, where he met <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a>. His account of the journey, printed in 1487, is a valuable source on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ambrogio-contarini.jpg" alt="Ambrogio Contarini" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ambrogio Contarini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viaggio_al_signor_Usun_Hassan_re_di_Persia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
